{"name":"Dragonflies","hex":"#c189bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dragonflies","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of dragonfly"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragonflies"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dragonflies (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Dragonflies is a 2022 Spanish drama film directed by Luc Knowles in his feature film debut which stars Milena Smit and Olivia Baglivi."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bd/Dragonflies_%28film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragonflies_(film)"},{"title":"Dragonflies (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Dragonflies is a British rock band formed by Dhani Harrison and Nigel Godrich. They released their debut album on September 18, 2026 via Dark Horse Records/BMG. The project unites Harrison—known for collaborations with thenewno2 and Fistful of Mercy, and who is the son of George Harrison—with musician and producer Nigel Godrich, known for his work with Radiohead, Beck, IDLES, Atoms for Peace and Ultraísta."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragonflies_(band)"},{"title":"Dragonfly","blocks":[{"text":"A dragonfly is a flying insect belonging to the suborder Anisoptera of the order Odonata. About 3,000 living species of dragonflies are known. Most are tropical, with fewer species in temperate regions. Loss of wetland habitat threatens dragonfly populations around the world. Adult dragonflies are characterised by a pair of large, multifaceted, compound eyes, two pairs of strong, transparent wings, sometimes with coloured patches, and an elongated body. Many dragonflies have brilliant iridescent or metallic colours produced by structural coloration, making them conspicuous in flight. An adult dragonfly's compound eyes have nearly 24,000 ommatidia each."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Red_grasshawk_%28Neurothemis_fluctuans%29_male_Phuket_2.jpg/330px-Red_grasshawk_%28Neurothemis_fluctuans%29_male_Phuket_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dragonfly"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Meganeura.png/500px-Meganeura.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Meganeura.png/1280px-Meganeura.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Meganeura.png/500px-Meganeura.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The giant Upper Carboniferous dragonfly relative, Meganeura monyi, attained a wingspan around 680 millimetres (27 inches).[8]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMeganeura.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mesurupetala%2C_dragonfly%2C_Late_Late_Jurassic%2C_Tithonian_Age%2C_Solnhofen_Lithographic_Limestone%2C_Solnhofen%2C_Bavaria%2C_Germany_-_Houston_Museum_of_Natural_Science_-_DSC01817.JPG/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mesurupetala%2C_dragonfly%2C_Late_Late_Jurassic%2C_Tithonian_Age%2C_Solnhofen_Lithographic_Limestone%2C_Solnhofen%2C_Bavaria%2C_Germany_-_Houston_Museum_of_Natural_Science_-_DSC01817.JPG/1280px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Mesurupetala%2C_dragonfly%2C_Late_Late_Jurassic%2C_Tithonian_Age%2C_Solnhofen_Lithographic_Limestone%2C_Solnhofen%2C_Bavaria%2C_Germany_-_Houston_Museum_of_Natural_Science_-_DSC01817.JPG/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mesurupetala, Late Jurassic (Tithonian), Solnhof